sequenceDiagram
    actor Author
    participant Sign as polar-sign
    participant Schema as Agent schema (--scaffold)
    participant Git as Git (policy clone)
    participant Server as Polar git server
    participant Cassini

    Note over Author,Schema: Once per agent: a typed template from the agent's own declarations
    Author->>Sign: template <agent>
    Sign->>Schema: read the agent's schema export
    Schema-->>Sign: every variable: type, default, secret, static or dynamic
    Sign-->>Author: Dhall record type of the Dynamic variables only

    Note over Author,Sign: Authoring: imports and templates are fine here
    Author->>Author: write item.dhall using the template

    Author->>Sign: check item.dhall
    Sign->>Sign: evaluate to normal form (no imports left)
    Sign->>Sign: parse each value with the agent's own declaration
    Sign->>Sign: version is above the last known, signing certificate valid and authorised
    Sign-->>Author: every problem at once, or OK

    Author->>Sign: sign item.dhall
    Sign->>Sign: canonical JSON of payload, domain prefix, ECDSA P-256 with the user's key
    Sign-->>Author: item.dhall rewritten as one file: payload and signature (signature and chain only)

    Note over Author,Git: Same key signs the commit, through git's x509 support (not a hook)
    Author->>Git: git commit
    Git->>Sign: gpg.x509.program: sign the commit object
    Sign-->>Git: detached signature
    Note right of Sign: setup wrote user.email from the certificate's mail

    Author->>Server: git push (mTLS with the user certificate)
    Server->>Server: authorise the pusher for this repository and branch
    opt repository requires signed commits
        Server->>Server: every pushed commit signed by the pusher's certificate, else refuse
    end
    Server-->>Author: accepted
    Server-)Cassini: RepoChanged {repo, ref, old, new, pusher}
